          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Please install the Fouine MCP server so you can search my documents. Run this command (it needs no administrator password):\n\n%@\n\nIt configures Claude Desktop, Claude Code, Cursor, Codex and Antigravity in one go and skips the clients that are not installed; other servers and settings are kept. Add `--client <name>` to configure a single client (claude-desktop, claude-code, cursor, codex, antigravity), `--dry-run` to preview what would be written, and `--folders <labels>` to serve only some of my folders. If your client is not in that list, `--print` gives the server entry to add to its configuration by hand. Add `--help` for the details.\n\nThe server is read-only: it never changes the index and never hands over my files. Once configured, restart the client so it picks up the server. The full guide, written for assistants: %@": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Please install the Fouine MCP server so you can search my documents. Run this command (it needs no administrator password):\n\n%@\n\nIt configures Claude Desktop, Claude Code, Cursor, Codex and Antigravity in one go and skips the clients that are not installed; other servers and settings are kept. Add `--client <name>` to configure a single client (claude-desktop, claude-code, cursor, codex, antigravity), `--dry-run` to preview what would be written, and `--folders <labels>` to serve only some of my folders. If your client is not in that list, `--print` gives the server entry to add to its configuration by hand. Add `--help` for the details.\n\nThe server is read-only: it never changes the index and never hands over my files. Once configured, restart the client so it picks up the server. The full guide, written for assistants: %@"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Installe le serveur MCP de Fouine, s’il te plaît, pour pouvoir chercher dans mes documents. Lance cette commande (elle ne demande aucun mot de passe d’administrateur) :\n\n%@\n\nElle configure Claude Desktop, Claude Code, Cursor, Codex et Antigravity d’un coup et saute les clients qui ne sont pas installés ; les autres serveurs et réglages sont conservés. Ajoute `--client <nom>` pour n’en configurer qu’un (claude-desktop, claude-code, cursor, codex, antigravity), `--dry-run` pour voir ce qui serait écrit sans rien écrire, et `--folders <étiquettes>` pour ne servir que certains de mes dossiers. Si ton client n’est pas dans cette liste, `--print` donne l’entrée du serveur à ajouter à sa configuration à la main. Ajoute `--help` pour le détail.\n\nLe serveur est en lecture seule : il ne modifie jamais l’index et ne livre jamais mes fichiers. Une fois configuré, relance le client pour qu’il voie le serveur. Le guide complet, écrit pour les assistants : %@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "To use Fouine with your AI assistant (Claude, Codex, Antigravity…), ask it to install the Fouine MCP!": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "To use Fouine with your AI assistant (Claude, Codex, Antigravity…), ask it to install the Fouine MCP!"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Pour utiliser Fouine avec votre assistant IA (Claude, Codex, Antigravity…), demandez-lui d’installer le MCP de Fouine !"
          }
        }
      }
    },
